     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">I think you have older version of R (and subsequently installed older version of ggplot)?<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Try to see what version you have, type:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">sessionInfo()<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">I have R-2.15.3 and ggplot2_0.9.3.1;  I don’t have any problem to run the code you posted below, but when I tested it with R-2.12.2 and ggplot2_0.8.9 then\r\n I got the same error as you have.  <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">--Kaori<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<div style=\"border:none;border-top:solid #b5c4df 1.0pt;padding:3.0pt 0in 0in 0in\">\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a>]\r\n<b>On Behalf Of </b>Genomics Epigenomics<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Wednesday, May 01, 2013 10:03 AM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Error: could not find function &quot;theme&quot;<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">After installing and loading ggplot2; <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">install.packages(&quot;ggplot2&quot;) <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">library(ggplot2)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I tried the following code,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&gt; p &lt;- qplot(mpg, wt, data = mtcars)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&gt; p + theme(panel.background = element_rect(colour = &quot;pink&quot;))<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">and got an error: Error: could not find function &quot;theme&quot;<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Any help please?<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thnx<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Nano<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">-- <br>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>\r\nPlease provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/devtools/wiki/Reproducibility&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792372909839000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1qn0xRpe1TjyMv9pbfzfbN\">\r\nhttps://github.com/hadley